            level axis carries 0.76 of one query's swing; most opposed pair -1.000
            'a red cube~' AND 'a green cube~' ARE EXACT NEGATIVES, so the LEVEL AXIS IS DEAD: lvl cannot
            move on any frame, M21's centring subtracts nothing, and both of its axes
            collapse to the raw pair. A MARGIN question still measures something -
            08-20 14:22 got a valid AUC this way - but every presence and level number
            in this run is void, and the enrolment guards cannot see it. Re-word one
            side so the two are not the same two phrases swapped (#25).
            scored as z = (cos - background) / std, where the background is this room's
            own mean over its first 30 frames and is then FROZEN - so a thing left in
            shot keeps its score instead of decaying into the furniture. 'N' re-learns
            it, 'H' switches to tracking. The COCO figures below are only the seed for
            frame 0 and the fixed std.
            std is THIS ROOM's, measured over the same 30 frames ('S' switches to COCO's).
            The thresholds below still mean the 90th percentile of a background; the
            background they now mean it against is this room empty, not 5000 COCO photos.
            z is EMA-smoothed at 0.35 (~5 frames) before ranking, so a state has to
            persist for about two seconds to be called.
            TWO-STAGE: the presence queries gate, and the state queries are then RANKED
            against each other with no threshold of their own - a contrast query's z
            is measured against an empty room, which is as much 'not an open hand' as
            a fist is, so it has no absolute level to clear. D1 reads the same two
            stages: brightness is the gate, red/green is which state leads.
            a red cube~          state, ranked; nominal z 1.23   (COCO background -0.015 +- 0.072, so cos 0.074)
            a green cube~        state, ranked; nominal z 1.23   (COCO background 0.015 +- 0.072, so cos 0.104)
            a block              match above z 1.23   (COCO background -0.122 +- 0.030, so cos -0.085)
            a toy block          match above z 1.23   (COCO background -0.154 +- 0.033, so cos -0.114)
            an object            match above z 1.23   (COCO background -0.124 +- 0.032, so cos -0.085)
            a cube               presence, gates above z 1.23   (COCO background -0.136 +- 0.030, so cos -0.100)

loop      : capture, 8 convs on the T8, pool and head, then one cosine per query. 'B' for BOOTSEL, 'R' to restart,
            'P' to dump the next frame for host/cam.py, 'V' to dump its 512 floats for host/caption.py,
            'E' to provoke a fault so D1 shows its fault display, 'H' to freeze/unfreeze the background,
            'S' to switch the spread between this room's and COCO's, 'W' to hang on purpose and see
            the watchdog name the stage, 'C' to stall the camera bus on purpose and see it cost one frame,
            'U' to drop off USB on purpose and watch it come back, 'I' to drop off and refuse to,
            'N' to forget it and learn it again from now. 'P' and 'V' together describe the same frame.
            'O' closes the timing window, prints it and flips the capture between overlapped and serial;
            'D' does the same and flips the trigger between late and at-the-collect, which is #14's A/B.
            'L' freezes the gain and nothing else - the AE ignores the mask on 32 boots of 33 and
            freezing the white balance drops the colour gains instead of holding them. A second press
            is the pre-09-07 arm (exposure + gain), a third and a fourth are the two ways to go green,
            a fifth restores. Issue #30, and the one hotkey whose answer depends on when you press it.
            Do not use two arms in one run: the unlock fails 31 times in 56, so the second arm is a
            camera sometimes still in the first.
            Every 'L' now prints what the sensor die did about it a few frames later, which is usually
            'nothing moved' and means nothing either way. 'K' asks the question that does answer, by
            writing an exposure and reading it back - it costs the frames around it, and a verdict of
            'held' can leave the sensor parked on the exposure it wrote. Issue #33.
            'M' goes further and takes the sensor OUT of the loop: the ArduChip feeds a fixed pattern, so
            the frame cannot drift for any reason. If the walk survives that, the walk is not the camera.
            Run it with the background frozen and z smoothing OFF, or the flat column is a filter and not a
            result. The pattern is not a photograph - judge the cosines it prints, not the z.
            scores are z against this room's background, ranked; '*' means over its threshold.
            '1'..'6' enrol the next 20 frames as that class, and press again on a LATER visit
            to fold a second one in - 2 visits is what makes the enrolment guard mean
            something. Two classes in and the board decides by nearest reference instead of
            by threshold - see M21.
            '0' ENROLS THE EMPTY SCENE the same way, and it is worth a visit: with one, a frame
            is absent when the empty reference is the nearest of the three and no radius is
            involved. Without one the board falls back to the band - absent beyond 2.0 sep
            from every class - which scores 53.8% over 33 benches against the third reference's
            79.4%, because with two queries that band is an interval the empty scene can sit
            inside. #18.
            'T' DUMPS THE ENROLMENT as text - the references, and the qbg and spread they were
            written against, which are the coordinate system and are re-measured every boot.
            Read-only: whether a saved reference means anything in the next boot is #34, and
            it is being measured before there is a way to load one back.
            'Y' FORGETS THE ENROLMENT AND KEEPS THE BACKGROUND, which is the half of 'N' that
            is safe: re-enrolling after it lands in the same coordinate system, so two
            references of one class become comparable. Pressing '1' twice does NOT do this -
            it folds a second visit into a running mean. #34.
            The first 30 frames set the baseline and it is then frozen, so anything left in
            shot KEEPS its score. Point the camera at the empty scene for those frames.
            Send a new set at any time to re-query - that resets the baseline too.

